        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Yes.\n\nSince $p,q,r>0$, every algebraic step in part (c) is reversible and recovers $P(A\\cap B)=P(A)P(B)$.",
          "worked": "Yes. With $p,q,r>0$, reverse the algebra in part (c) to obtain\n$$2p(q+r)=(2p-p^2)\\,2(pq+pr+qr).$$\nThe left side is $P(A\\cap B)$ and the right side is $P(A)P(B)$. Therefore $A$ and $B$ are independent.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
