        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Subspecies Y only.\n\nThe criterion from part (d) gives $\\frac32$ for X and $1$ for Y.",
          "worked": "For Subspecies X,\n$$\\begin{align*}(q+r)\\left(\\frac qr+\\frac rq+1\\right)&=\\left(\\frac14+\\frac14\\right)(1+1+1)\\\\(q+r)\\left(\\frac qr+\\frac rq+1\\right)&=\\frac32\\ne1.\\end{align*}$$\nThus the events are dependent in X.\nFor Subspecies Y,\n$$\\begin{align*}(q+r)\\left(\\frac qr+\\frac rq+1\\right)&=\\left(\\frac16+\\frac16\\right)(1+1+1)\\\\(q+r)\\left(\\frac qr+\\frac rq+1\\right)&=1.\\end{align*}$$\nBy part (d), being partly pink is independent of being striped in Subspecies Y only.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
